@startuml

start

:Power management subsystem monitors voltage rails via PMIC and BMS;
:Execute predefined protection;
:Execute recovery policies;

if (Detect anomalous sensor data?) then (yes)
  :Initiate data verification sequence;

  if (Verification fails?) then (yes)
    :Trigger fault isolation routine;
    :Check sensor hardware connection;
    :Check data uplink channel integrity via CAN;
    :Check power rail stability;

    if (Any check fails?) then (yes)
      :Activate redundant sensor path;
      :Spawn deterministically parallel processing tasks;
      :Managed by RTOS scheduler using priority queues and mutexes;
      :Protect shared resource;
       fork
      :Timer ISR drives periodic sampling from redundant path;
      fork again
      :Process data through protected ring buffer;
      end fork

      :Parallel task completion;
      :Initialize second-stage recovery mechanism;

      repeat
        :Execute concurrent data repair algorithms within dedicated RTOS tasks;
      repeat while(Data integrity restored) is(no)

    else (no)
    end if

  else (no)
  end if

else (no)
end if

:Watchdog timer is serviced;
:Hardware events are debounced;
:State transitions are logged;
:Ensure monitoring data accuracy and overall system stability;

stop

@enduml
